Relevant tables / columns for the final request
------------------------------------------------
• director_mapping.movie_id : movie identifier to be linked with movies / ratings  
• director_mapping.name_id  : director identifier (to be grouped)

• names.id                 : joins with director_mapping.name_id  
• names.name               : human‑readable director name to be returned

• movies.id                : joins with director_mapping.movie_id  
• movies.duration          : single‑movie running time (minutes)  
  Possible filter → WHERE movies.duration IS NOT NULL

• ratings.movie_id         : joins with director_mapping.movie_id  
• ratings.avg_rating       : rating for one movie (needed for avg / min / max)  
• ratings.total_votes      : number of votes (needed for SUM)  
  Possible filter → WHERE ratings.avg_rating IS NOT NULL

Basic conditions that will usually be applied
---------------------------------------------
1) director_mapping.movie_id = movies.id  
2) director_mapping.movie_id = ratings.movie_id  
3) director_mapping.name_id  = names.id  
4) Aggregate by director_mapping.name_id (and names.name)  
5) HAVING COUNT(*) > 0                                     -- (movie count)

10 probing / building‑block queries
-----------------------------------

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at how movie IDs map to directors (20 random rows).
SELECT DISTINCT "movie_id", "name_id"
FROM "director_mapping"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Get a list of unique directors with their human names.
SELECT DISTINCT dm."name_id", n."name"
FROM   "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN   "names"            AS n  ON dm."name_id" = n."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Inspect durations available for films that have a director entry.
SELECT DISTINCT m."id", m."duration"
FROM   "movies"            AS m
JOIN   "director_mapping"  AS dm ON dm."movie_id" = m."id"
WHERE  m."duration" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Inspect ratings that belong to movies with directors.
SELECT DISTINCT r."movie_id", r."avg_rating", r."total_votes"
FROM   "ratings"           AS r
JOIN   "director_mapping"  AS dm ON dm."movie_id" = r."movie_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Simple movie count per director (top 20).
SELECT dm."name_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "movie_count"
FROM   "director_mapping" AS dm
GROUP  BY dm."name_id"
ORDER  BY "movie_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Combine movie count and total duration per director.
SELECT dm."name_id",
       COUNT(*)              AS "movie_count",
       SUM(m."duration")     AS "total_duration"
FROM   "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN   "movies"            AS m ON dm."movie_id" = m."id"
GROUP  BY dm."name_id"
ORDER  BY "movie_count" DESC, "total_duration" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Add average, min, max rating & vote totals per director.
SELECT dm."name_id",
       COUNT(*)                      AS "movie_count",
       ROUND(AVG(r."avg_rating"),2)  AS "avg_rating",
       MIN(r."avg_rating")           AS "min_rating",
       MAX(r."avg_rating")           AS "max_rating",
       SUM(r."total_votes")          AS "total_votes"
FROM   "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN   "ratings"          AS r ON dm."movie_id" = r."movie_id"
GROUP  BY dm."name_id"
ORDER  BY "movie_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Calculate average inter‑movie duration per director.
--   (Average of durations, rounded to nearest int.)
SELECT dm."name_id",
       ROUND(AVG(m."duration")) AS "avg_duration"
FROM   "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN   "movies"            AS m ON dm."movie_id" = m."id"
GROUP  BY dm."name_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Bring together all metrics except the director’s name.
SELECT dm."name_id",
       COUNT(*)                              AS "movie_count",
       ROUND(AVG(m."duration"))              AS "avg_duration",
       ROUND(AVG(r."avg_rating"), 2)         AS "avg_rating",
       SUM(r."total_votes")                  AS "total_votes",
       MIN(r."avg_rating")                   AS "min_rating",
       MAX(r."avg_rating")                   AS "max_rating",
       SUM(m."duration")                     AS "total_duration"
FROM   "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN   "movies"            AS m ON dm."movie_id" = m."id"
JOIN   "ratings"           AS r ON dm."movie_id" = r."movie_id"
GROUP  BY dm."name_id"
ORDER  BY "movie_count" DESC, "total_duration" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final query adding the director name and limiting to the top 9.
SELECT dm."name_id"                           AS "director_id",
       n."name"                               AS "director_name",
       COUNT(*)                               AS "movie_count",
       ROUND(AVG(m."duration"))               AS "avg_duration",
       ROUND(AVG(r."avg_rating"), 2)          AS "avg_rating",
       SUM(r."total_votes")                   AS "total_votes",
       MIN(r."avg_rating")                    AS "min_rating",
       MAX(r."avg_rating")                    AS "max_rating",
       SUM(m."duration")                      AS "total_duration"
FROM   "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN   "names"            AS n ON dm."name_id" = n."id"
JOIN   "movies"           AS m ON dm."movie_id" = m."id"
JOIN   "ratings"          AS r ON dm."movie_id" = r."movie_id"
GROUP  BY dm."name_id", n."name"
ORDER  BY "movie_count" DESC, "total_duration" DESC
LIMIT 9;
```
